# Project startup impact review (2 October 2026)

- Literal: connect global doctrine to automatic TMP, memory, feedback and cloud preparation. Inverse: instructions alone cannot initialize a watcher. Adjacent: retries, concurrent sessions and existing production links. Reframed: agents execute one verified preparation command before producing files. (2 October 2026)
- Risk 1, existing mappings lost: start previously rebuilt only workshop and project-notes. Corrected by retaining all registered sources and dependencies; tests preserve a Houdini source and zenray-shards-core dependency on the second start. (2 October 2026)
- Risk 2, two agents lose a session binding: SessionBindings.json was read and rewritten without a lock. Corrected with session-bindings.lock; concurrent binding test verifies both entries persist. (2 October 2026)
- Risk 3, feedback written to another directory: initialization now rejects symlink ancestors and non-regular canonical feedback. Negative test verifies no AGENTS.md appears in the outside target. (2 October 2026)
- Risk 4, global rules become truncated: CLAUDE.md measured 58437 bytes against 65536, leaving 7099. Project metadata stays in Project.json and the Assets registry rather than appending every new project to global doctrine. extract-rules.mjs --verify passes. (2 October 2026)
- Risk 5, partial setup mistaken for a cloud backup: BeginProject.mjs fails visibly if the bridge or setup fails, and reports watched/sessionBound separately. Local-only status persists until the independent archive proof; two stable seconds are not claimed as a finished cloud upload. (2 October 2026)
- Premortem: three weeks later an agent resumes Louisiana with a new id and forks its history; the global rule requires reusing the existing identity. A second incident would replace a human AGENTS.md; initialization uses exclusive creation and tests retain its exact old contents. (2 October 2026)
- Verdict: GO for prepared, registered projects. Unregistered mixed folders, portable scene dependencies and complete capture of every agent environment remain outside the proof. Existing state, concurrency, partial failure, scope, observability and reversal are checked; payment and public API changes are not involved. (2 October 2026)
